ow: an AP that is not running starts on its backhaul station's channel

opensync-rpi / opensync-lab: the STA channel override left an AP that is not running (not
yet started, or being restarted) alone, so it started on its configured channel. Patch
0008 moves an AP whose CSA hostapd refuses by restarting its BSS; the restart came back on
the configured channel, the override then asked for the station's channel again, and the
AP restarted about once a minute (both Raspberry Pi pods after the physical MV3 moved from
channel 6 to 2, 2026-10-09 09:52Z). With a station linked on the radio, an AP that is not
running now takes the station's channel, so it starts there and needs no move at all.
The decision is in ow_sta_channel_override_action.h, free of the module's state, so that
pod/opensync/tests/ow_sta_channel_override_action_test.c tests it on its own; live: the
pods' APs on the MV3's channel after a move, without restarts.

Upstream: an OpenSync core behaviour as released in 6.6.1.0:
ow_sta_channel_override_ap_get_action() in src/lib/ow/src/ow_sta_channel_override.c
returns DONT_CHANGE for an AP that is not running, so an AP (re)started while its radio's
station is on another channel starts away from it. Not reported (the owner decides).

